From bb15f392fc6dea81f18899aa557346cddfc60471 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:27:32 +0000
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: CBM probe and datapath bring-up orchestration

Add cbm.c: the platform driver for the cbm@1e700000 node and the
bring-up sequence tying together everything added so far. The order
below is the hardware-verified one (TX and RX both proven on a
FRITZ!Box 7560); the marked constraints are load-bearing.

Probe sequence:

 1. ioremap the twelve register windows from the DT; log (never
    write) the CGU gate state - the boot chain's clock/gate state
    is preserved throughout.
 2. Map the reserved-memory buffer pools.
 3. TOE/DMA3 controller reset parity (matching the vendor hdma
    probe environment) BEFORE the CBM hardware init.
 4. cbm_hw_init: interconnect endianness/mux parity writes
    (IPT endian select, IFMUX TX-path bits, watchdog-reset
    enables), FSQM init for both segment sizes, init_cbm_basic
    (pool base registers incl. the IOCU aliases, JSEL, counter
    zero-fill, interrupt mapping and the five request_irq calls -
    CBM IRQs are live from this point), EQM CPU ports 0-3 (must
    precede the first FSQM buffer pop), EQM DMA ingress ports 5-8
    standard+jumbo with descriptor seeds, the TOE (IGP9) and LDMA
    (IGP15) ports, and setup_DMA_p2p() - request the DMA1TX/DMA2RX
    channel pair, seed the shared 32-descriptor ring and p2p-pair
    them. The unseeded ring was the final RX blocker: the bridge
    silently moves nothing without owned, buffer-backed
    descriptors.
 5. tmu_init().
 6. QIDT baseline: fill the whole queue-selection cube with the
    drop value, then run the CPU DQM row walk (queues 35/34/36)
    and the endpoint-7 route to queue 35 - routes are carved out
    of an all-drop baseline, never the reverse.
 7. cbm_rx_engine_init() - RX tasklets armed before any channel
    can deliver.
 8. Preconfigure the LAN TX dequeue port (DQM DMA port 10) and its
    flat TMU egress path at probe time; record the preconfig so
    cbm_dp_enable() does not redo it. Egress must be configured
    BEFORE the controllers are enabled.
 9. cbm_enable_controllers(): DQM enable, load-spreader init, EQM
    enable, then the enqueue-delay setting that lets the TMU bind
    body lengths.
10. hdma_port_enable(10): open the DMA2TX egress channel once, at
    the end of probe, after the TMU egress port exists - the
    channel is never toggled afterwards (toggling it desynchronizes
    the dequeue handshake).
11. Open the eight EQM RX-admit movers: DMA2RX ch14/15 (standard)
    and ch30/31 (jumbo) into IGP5/6, DMA1RX ch0/6 into IGP7 and
    ch5/11 into IGP8 - DMA1RX ch0 is the actual host-RX admit
    mover.

turn_on_DMA_p2p() (called from ndo_open) switches the seeded bridge
pair on exactly once.

Derived from the AVM FRITZ!Box 7560 GPL release (Linux 4.9.198),
cqm/grx500/cbm.c probe/config-walk code (no vendor copyright
banners in the origin; provenance recorded per-function in
comments). Deviations from the vendor order (EQM armed earlier)
were proven benign on hardware; deviations in the marked
constraints were each observed to break TX or RX.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
